# The site repository is PUBLIC and holds only the built site: everything is ignored except the four paths below, so `git add .` can never pick up
# anything else (app code, an .env file, keys, notes). Use `git add -f` on purpose only if you really mean it (you should not).
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/.github/
!/public/
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.jks
*.p12
